<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nyatsimba Mutota</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mutota</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nyatsimba Mutota was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> in the fifteenth century. A prince of the declining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-zimbabwe">Kingdom of Zimbabwe</a>, he migrated northwards in search of salt and fertile land. He established authority over local Shona-speaking communities and laid the foundation of a centralised state between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> rivers.</p></div>
